# One of the seventy impaired vectors of vendor/hydramodem-rx/ (ADR 0014
# decision 2; docs/design/receptor.md D11). stdin is the WAV; the expectation
# is HydraModem's OWN receiver's verdict on the same bytes, recorded in
# vendor/hydramodem-rx/verdicta.tsv when the tree was vendored and not
# re-derived here.
#
# The exemplum frame resampled by +500 ppm -- a transmitter and a receiver
# whose clocks disagree by that much. R2 sampled on a fixed 48-sample
# grid and this is one of the inputs that walks off it; D10's timing
# loop is what follows it.
#
# The reference decodes it to its own frame,
# so this directory expects exit 0 and expected.out -- the seventeen bytes
# of d31312340001ffffdeadbeefab12cd24c0, compared by `cmp`. Where this
# receiver refuses instead, check_run's "wrote nothing, expected 17 bytes"
# is the half of the assertion that fails.
#
# This directory is generated, one per vector, and its verdict is the
# certificate ADR 0014 decision 1 states: decode everything the reference
# decodes, and never write a frame that is not the input's. A refusal where the
# reference also refused is fine; a refusal where it succeeded is a failure of
# this certificate, and a WRONG frame is a failure of the stronger half.
TEST: expect-exit=0 stdin=vendor/hydramodem-rx/clock/exemplum-p0500ppm.wav sources=examples/hydramodem/quantum.exsc,examples/hydramodem/modulator.exsc,examples/hydramodem/receptor.exsc,examples/hydramodem/recipe.exsc c-differentia=nightly-sweep
